-- Maximum Subarray Sum
INSERT INTO problems (slug, title, description, constraints, difficulty, time_limit_ms, memory_limit_mb, published) VALUES ($q$maximum-subarray-sum$q$, $q$Maximum Subarray Sum$q$, $q$Given an array of `n` integers, find the largest possible sum of a **non-empty contiguous** subarray.

### Input
- The first line contains `n`.
- The second line contains `n` space-separated integers.

### Output
Print the maximum subarray sum.$q$, $q$- `1 <= n <= 2 * 10^5`
- `-10^9 <= a[i] <= 10^9`
- Use 64-bit integers for the running sum.$q$, $q$MEDIUM$q$, 1000, 256, TRUE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
