-- Count the Islands
INSERT INTO problems (slug, title, description, constraints, difficulty, time_limit_ms, memory_limit_mb, published) VALUES ($q$count-islands$q$, $q$Count the Islands$q$, $q$A map is a grid of `0` (water) and `1` (land). An **island** is a maximal group of land cells connected horizontally or vertically (not diagonally).

Count the islands on the map.

### Input
- The first line contains `R` and `C`, the number of rows and columns.
- The next `R` lines each contain a string of `C` characters, each `0` or `1`.

### Output
Print the number of islands.$q$, $q$- `1 <= R, C <= 1000`$q$, $q$MEDIUM$q$, 1500, 256, TRUE) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
